e (regime switch) from the available temporal evidence. The per-subwindow event counts (step_03) show activity for the group is distributed across the interval without a single short, large transition that would clearly indicate an abrupt replacement of partner sets. The nodes are relatively active/popular (distinct partner counts in step_02) and, when time is ignored, many shared neighbours appear in the first-half neighbor lists (steps_04\u201308) \u2014 each of these are alternative explanations that could mask or mimic a regime switch. Crucially, I could not obtain comparable neighbour identities for a later subinterval to demonstrate an old set giving way to a new set in a short transition, so the temporal evidence is insufficient to conclude presence or absence of a regime_switch."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8b4a3bfa\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776],\n  \"window\": [246, 30246],\n  \"confidence\": 0.30,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"I cannot reliably determine an abrupt partner-change (regime switch) from the available temporal evidence. The per-subwindow event counts (step_03) show activity for the group is distributed across the interval without a single short, large transition that would clearly indicate an abrupt replacement of partner sets. The nodes are relatively active/popular (distinct partner counts in step_02) and, when time is ignore